// Synthetic m1-eval multirate fixture. No proprietary content.
// 50 Hz: writes Slow Out = Seed * 2. The 100 Hz Fast Writer reads Slow Out
// across rates. The planner keeps that dependency when both functions are due,
// and the fast function reads a held value on odd base ticks.
// Also writes Slow Echo (= Seed * 2) which NOTHING reads: a clean probe for the
// zero-order-hold path outside dependency ordering.
Slow Out = Seed * 2.0;
Slow Echo = Seed * 2.0;
